{"name":"Ghost Pepper","hex":"#c10102","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ghost pepper","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Synonym of bhut jolokia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ghost_pepper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ghost pepper","blocks":[{"text":"The ghost pepper, also known as bhut jolokia or naga jolokia, is a superhot chili pepper cultivated in Northeast India.\nIn 2007, Guinness World Records certified that the ghost pepper was the world's hottest chili pepper, 170 times hotter than Tabasco sauce. The ghost chili is rated at more than one million Scoville Heat Units (SHUs) and far surpasses the amount of a habanero. However, the ghost chili has since been superseded by the Trinidad Scorpion Butch T pepper in 2011, the Carolina Reaper in 2013 and Pepper X in 2023."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Bhut-Jolokia-pc.jpg/330px-Bhut-Jolokia-pc.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost_pepper","wikidata":"Q426850"},{"title":"Ghost","blocks":[{"text":"In folklore, a ghost is the soul or spirit of a dead person or non-human animal that is believed by some people to be able to appear to the living. In ghostlore, descriptions of ghosts vary widely, from an invisible presence to translucent or barely visible wispy shapes to realistic, lifelike forms, whether they resemble humans or animals. The deliberate attempt to contact the spirit of a deceased person is known as necromancy, or in spiritism as a séance. Other terms associated with it are apparition, haunt, haint, phantom, poltergeist, shade, specter, spirit, spook, wraith, demon, and ghoul."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/02/Hammersmith_Ghost.PNG/330px-Hammersmith_Ghost.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost","wikidata":"Q45529"}],"images":[{"srcset":"http